          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Verify Ubuntu 24.04 LTS generates an audit record upon successful/unsuccessful attempts to use the "chown", "fchown", "fchownat", and "lchown" system calls with the following command:
 
$ sudo auditctl -l | grep chown
-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -S chown,fchown,fchownat,lchown -F auid&gt;=1000 -F auid!=-1 -k perm_chng 
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S chown,fchown,fchownat,lchown -F auid&gt;=1000 -F auid!=-1 -k perm_chng 
 
If the command does not return audit rules for the "chown", "fchown", "fchownat", and "lchown" syscalls or the lines are commented out, this is a finding. 
 
Notes: 
- For 32-bit architectures, only the 32-bit specific output lines from the commands are required. 
- The "-k" allows for specifying an arbitrary identifier, and the string after it does not need to match the example output above.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
